<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Danish KFK lowers 97 expectations.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Danish KFK lowers 97 expectations.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Danish grain and feedstuffs wholesaler A/S Korn og Foderstof Kompagniet (KFK) downgraded on Tuesday its full-year expectations to the level of 1996 results.</p>
<p>In February, KFK posted a disappointing 1996 net profit of 75 million crowns, dramatically lower than the previous year's 191 million crowns but foresaw &quot;a somewhat better&quot; 1997 result.</p>
<p>The firm said that 1997's first quarter did not meet expectations, with higher raw material prices and late spring sewing meaning delayed seed and fertiliser sales.</p>
<p>-- Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
